 ### Color Palette Sparsity Loss
-Adopted from PaletteNeRF, this loss measures the sparsity of the learned color palette $\hat{P}$. Formula: $\mathcal{L}_{\text {sp}} = \frac {\sum _{i=1}^{N_{\hat{P}}} \hat{w}_i}{\sum _{i=1}^{N_{\hat{P}}} \hat{w}_i^2} - 1$, where $\hat{w}_i$ is the per-palette weight. [S7]
