 ## Background
-Loss function configuration has evolved alongside radiance field optimization. Standard 3DGS uses SSIM (weight 0.8) and L1 (weight 0.2) [S4]. Subsequent works introduced stage-specific weighting [S2], hybrid gradient strategies [S6], and specialized regularizations for specific tasks like relighting [S1, unofficial], dynamic scenes [S2], and stylization [S8]. The removal of redundant terms (like repulsion loss in sphere-guided methods [S3]) and the introduction of entropy-based separation [S10] reflect ongoing efforts to stabilize and improve the fidelity of differentiable volume rendering.
